cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RAF, please cite it as below."
title: "RAF — Rust Agentic Foundations"
abstract: >-
  RAF is a set of Rust libraries and cargo subcommands that Blackcat projects
  use as dev-dependencies to keep a code base and its documentation honest.
  raf-census finds structurally duplicated code under a versioned normal form
  and holds it against a ledger; raf-workplan plans changes to documented
  capabilities and refuses to complete a change until the capability documents
  state the delivered contract. raf-okf reads and validates the Markdown and
  YAML documents, and raf-source indexes Rust source for both.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Blackcat Informatics® Inc."
    website: "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/"
version: "0.1.0"
license:
